From 7de7c8fb322239a6fca44bcd88ec0be01e655c20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:08:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] signal: drop the unsafe stdio calls from do_reboot()

do_reboot() has exactly one caller, signal_crash(), so every statement
in it runs inside a SIGSEGV or SIGBUS handler. Neither fflush() nor
ulog() is async-signal-safe: both take a lock, so a crash raised inside
any stdio or syslog call deadlocks procd against itself instead of
rebooting the box. The flush has had nothing to flush since procd's own
messages stopped travelling on stderr, and the line it announced is now
written to /dev/kmsg by the caller. Only sync(), sleep() and reboot()
remain.

Fixes: f1bf99b09f66 ("add signal handler")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
(cherry picked from commit 46dc5e51faed205bda5514e03a70136a50add9f9)
---
 signal.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/signal.c b/signal.c
index b9fa0bc..3c44ee3 100644
--- a/signal.c
+++ b/signal.c
@@ -47,8 +47,6 @@ static void crash_kmsg(void)
 
 static void do_reboot(void)
 {
-	LOG("reboot\n");
-	fflush(stderr);
 	sync();
 	sleep(2);
 	reboot(RB_AUTOBOOT);
